{"sequence": 10, "time_s": 5.329, "type": "evidence", "evidence": {"evidence_id": "d1s0", "title": "Eysteinn", "url": "https://trace.invalid/2wikimultihopqa_87a90ac60bb011ebab90acde48001122_short/d1s0", "text": "Eysteinn (Swedish: Östen; died ca 600) was the son of Eadgils and Yrsa of Saxony.", "visible_time_s": 5.3289999999979045, "requested_subject": "", "resolved_title": "Eysteinn", "entity_resolution": "unspecified"}}
{"sequence": 11, "time_s": 5.329, "type": "evidence", "evidence": {"evidence_id": "d1s1", "title": "Eysteinn", "url": "https://trace.invalid/2wikimultihopqa_87a90ac60bb011ebab90acde48001122_short/d1s1", "text": "He was the father of Ingvar.", "visible_time_s": 5.3289999999979045, "requested_subject": "", "resolved_title": "Eysteinn", "entity_resolution": "unspecified"}}
{"sequence": 12, "time_s": 5.329, "type": "evidence", "evidence": {"evidence_id": "d1s2", "title": "Eysteinn", "url": "https://trace.invalid/2wikimultihopqa_87a90ac60bb011ebab90acde48001122_short/d1s2", "text": "The Eysteinn tumulus \"(Östens hög)\" in Västerås near Östanbro has been linked to King Eysteinn by some popular historians.", "visible_time_s": 5.3289999999979045, "requested_subject": "", "resolved_title": "Eysteinn", "entity_resolution": "unspecified"}}
{"sequence": 13, "time_s": 5.329, "type": "evidence", "evidence": {"evidence_id": "d1s3", "title": "Eysteinn", "url": "https://trace.invalid/2wikimultihopqa_87a90ac60bb011ebab90acde48001122_short/d1s3", "text": "The term Hög is derived from the Old Norse word \"haugr\" meaning mound or barrow.", "visible_time_s": 5.3289999999979045, "requested_subject": "", "resolved_title": "Eysteinn", "entity_resolution": "unspecified"}}
{"sequence": 14, "time_s": 5.329, "type": "evidence", "evidence": {"evidence_id": "d1s4", "title": "Eysteinn", "url": "https://trace.invalid/2wikimultihopqa_87a90ac60bb011ebab90acde48001122_short/d1s4", "text": "Eysteinn ruled Sweden at the time when Hrólf Kraki died in Lejre.", "visible_time_s": 5.3289999999979045, "requested_subject": "", "resolved_title": "Eysteinn", "entity_resolution": "unspecified"}}
{"sequence": 15, "time_s": 5.329, "type": "evidence", "evidence": {"evidence_id": "d1s5", "title": "Eysteinn", "url": "https://trace.invalid/2wikimultihopqa_87a90ac60bb011ebab90acde48001122_short/d1s5", "text": "It was a troubled time when many sea kings ravaged Swedish shores.", "visible_time_s": 5.3289999999979045, "requested_subject": "", "resolved_title": "Eysteinn", "entity_resolution": "unspecified"}}
{"sequence": 16, "time_s": 5.329, "type": "evidence", "evidence": {"evidence_id": "d1s6", "title": "Eysteinn", "url": "https://trace.invalid/2wikimultihopqa_87a90ac60bb011ebab90acde48001122_short/d1s6", "text": "One of those kings was named Sölve and he was from Jutland (but according to \"Historia Norwegiae\" he was Geatish, see below).", "visible_time_s": 5.3289999999979045, "requested_subject": "", "resolved_title": "Eysteinn", "entity_resolution": "unspecified"}}
{"sequence": 17, "time_s": 5.329, "type": "evidence", "evidence": {"evidence_id": "d1s7", "title": "Eysteinn", "url": "https://trace.invalid/2wikimultihopqa_87a90ac60bb011ebab90acde48001122_short/d1s7", "text": "At this time Sölve was pillaging in the Baltic Sea.", "visible_time_s": 5.3289999999979045, "requested_subject": "", "resolved_title": "Eysteinn", "entity_resolution": "unspecified"}}
{"sequence": 18, "time_s": 5.329, "type": "evidence", "evidence": {"evidence_id": "d1s8", "title": "Eysteinn", "url": "https://trace.invalid/2wikimultihopqa_87a90ac60bb011ebab90acde48001122_short/d1s8", "text": "He arrived in Lofond (probably the island of Lovön or the Lagunda Hundred), where Eysteinn was at a feast.", "visible_time_s": 5.3289999999979045, "requested_subject": "", "resolved_title": "Eysteinn", "entity_resolution": "unspecified"}}
{"sequence": 19, "time_s": 5.329, "type": "evidence", "evidence": {"evidence_id": "d1s9", "title": "Eysteinn", "url": "https://trace.invalid/2wikimultihopqa_87a90ac60bb011ebab90acde48001122_short/d1s9", "text": "Sölve and his men surrounded the house and set it on fire burning everyone inside to death.", "visible_time_s": 5.3289999999979045, "requested_subject": "", "resolved_title": "Eysteinn", "entity_resolution": "unspecified"}}
{"sequence": 20, "time_s": 5.329, "type": "evidence", "evidence": {"evidence_id": "d1s10", "title": "Eysteinn", "url": "https://trace.invalid/2wikimultihopqa_87a90ac60bb011ebab90acde48001122_short/d1s10", "text": "Then Sölve arrived at Sigtuna (Old Sigtuna) and ordered the Swedes to accept him as king.", "visible_time_s": 5.3289999999979045, "requested_subject": "", "resolved_title": "Eysteinn", "entity_resolution": "unspecified"}}
